        "explain": "Imagine a bank robbery where the street camera only sees a black sedan driving away, the lobby camera only sees a masked individual in a hoodie, and the bank vault sensor only records a code entered at 2:00 AM. If three separate detectives look at those three clues independently, none of them solve the crime. But when one detective connects the timeline—the code was used at 2:00 AM, the hooded figure exited at 2:03 AM, and the black sedan sped away at 2:04 AM—the crime is solved. In cybersecurity, **no single log source tells the whole story**. An incident is only solved when you correlate host, network, identity, and cloud logs together.",
